{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — a "+" item: secondary information in an overlay.

  Aloha, 8 October 2026 (product page notes):

    "Anything marked with a "+" is interactive. On desktop I don't want these
     sections opening downwards and making the whole page longer. The idea is
     that when someone hovers/clicks the +, a small simple overlay/window
     appears with the information. When they move away or close it, the page
     returns exactly as it is."

    "On mobile … the + should work by tap. My preference would be a small
     drawer/panel that opens over the page, rather than a long accordion
     pushing all the content underneath further down. Just a simple
     background colour of #F8F5ED. Tap "+" > info panel opens > x / close or
     tap outside > product page back to visibility."

  So this replaces the accordion rows (snippets/ha-panel-row) on the product
  page. The trigger is a line in the page; the panel never takes space in the
  layout. assets/ha-info-pop.js moves every panel to <body> on load (so a
  sticky, scrolling rail cannot clip it) and drives it:

    desktop (a mouse, 990px and wider)  hover opens a small window beside the
                                        "+"; leaving closes it. A click pins
                                        it open until ×, Escape or a click
                                        elsewhere.
    touch / narrower screens            tap opens a panel over the page from
                                        the foot of the screen, on #F8F5ED;
                                        ×, Escape or a tap outside closes it.

  Without JavaScript the panel stays where it is and simply shows, so nothing
  is ever out of reach.

  `content` is already-rendered HTML — capture it at the call site:

    {%- capture body -%}…{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- render 'ha-info-pop', id: 'description', title: 'Description', content: body -%}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign pop_id = 'ha-pop-' | append: id
  assign pop_title_id = pop_id | append: '-title'
-%}

{%- if content != blank -%}
  <div class="ha-pop{% if class != blank %} {{ class }}{% endif %}" data-ha-pop>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="ha-pop__trigger"
      aria-expanded="false"
      aria-controls="{{ pop_id }}"
      aria-haspopup="dialog"
    >
      <span class="ha-pop__label">{{ title }}</span>
      <span class="ha-pop__plus" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </button>
    <div
      class="ha-pop__panel"
      id="{{ pop_id }}"
      role="dialog"
      aria-labelledby="{{ pop_title_id }}"
      data-smooth-prevent
    >
      <div class="ha-pop__head">
        <p class="ha-pop__name" id="{{ pop_title_id }}">{{ title }}</p>
        <button type="button" class="ha-pop__close" data-ha-pop-close aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t | default: 'Close' }}"></button>
      </div>
      <div class="ha-pop__body">
        {{ content }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
